WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.032 --> 00:00:04.921
- So what do you think holds people back?

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:06.723
They know what they want to do,

00:00:06.723 --> 00:00:08.284
but they just can't keep the habit.

00:00:08.284 --> 00:00:09.798
They do it once and then
they fall off the train,

00:00:09.798 --> 00:00:11.375
and then next month they do it again

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:12.391
and they fall off the train.

00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:14.494
How do you make that consistent?

00:00:14.494 --> 00:00:18.511
- Well, you just keep working
at it and working at it.

00:00:18.511 --> 00:00:22.040
The best way of all is
to plan it in advance.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.067
Instead of sitting down,

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.606
never start work without a list,

00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:27.352
and never start work without
prioritizing your list.

00:00:27.352 --> 00:00:28.763
People sit down and they say

00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:31.467
well before I make a list
I'll check a little email,

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.156
check a little spam.

00:00:33.156 --> 00:00:34.616
I'll send something to my friend.

00:00:34.616 --> 00:00:37.674
See what' going on YouTube
and so on and so forth.

00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:39.851
And then they look up
and it's ten o'clock.

00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:41.947
And they haven't got anything of value.

00:00:41.947 --> 00:00:45.197
So what you do is you have to do is say

00:00:47.073 --> 00:00:49.323
well, if you start it right

00:00:51.077 --> 00:00:53.547
it'll work out right.

00:00:53.547 --> 00:00:56.553
So start it on your most important task.

00:00:56.553 --> 00:00:58.780
And do that until it becomes a habit.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.557
Here's an interesting
thing about checking email.

00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:04.237
Is when you check email,

00:01:04.237 --> 00:01:07.997
it triggers the release
of dopamine in your brain.

00:01:07.997 --> 00:01:09.496
Dopamine is a drug.

00:01:09.496 --> 00:01:11.912
By the way there's all
kinds of books and articles

00:01:11.912 --> 00:01:13.782
and scientific studies on this.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:17.050
And dopamine is the same drug in cocaine.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.288
What it does is it's triggered every time

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:23.350
you have a shiny object or something new

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.676
or different or interesting or sparkly.

00:01:25.676 --> 00:01:27.297
If a telephone rings next to you,

00:01:27.297 --> 00:01:28.271
you go bing.

00:01:28.271 --> 00:01:30.032
Your brain releases endorphins

00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:32.161
and you can't hardly
wait to see what it is.

00:01:32.161 --> 00:01:33.610
So you're talking to somebody,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.112
and you could be talking to somebody

00:01:35.112 --> 00:01:36.194
about something very serious,

00:01:36.194 --> 00:01:37.593
and your telephone goes off.

00:01:37.593 --> 00:01:38.426
Bing.

00:01:38.426 --> 00:01:40.276
Your whole mind goes blank.

00:01:40.276 --> 00:01:42.393
The middle of conversation stops.

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:43.423
You grab for your phone.

00:01:43.423 --> 00:01:44.256
You pick it up.

00:01:44.256 --> 00:01:45.089
You look at it.

00:01:45.089 --> 00:01:46.514
You check it out and everything else.

00:01:46.514 --> 00:01:47.698
And then you come back.

00:01:47.698 --> 00:01:48.894
If you're working on a task,

00:01:48.894 --> 00:01:50.759
it takes an average of seventeen minutes

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:52.243
to get back to the task.

00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:54.243
And then there's another distraction.

00:01:54.243 --> 00:01:56.051
So another seventeen minutes.

00:01:56.051 --> 00:02:00.290
Average adult is checking
their email and their phone

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.493
between 95 and 145 times a day.

00:02:03.493 --> 00:02:04.764
- That's crazy.

00:02:04.764 --> 00:02:09.009
- Which means they're like
attention-deficit disorder dogs.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:10.653
They're just living running around

00:02:10.653 --> 00:02:11.568
back and forth the whole day.

00:02:11.568 --> 00:02:12.914
The end of the day they're exhausted.

00:02:12.914 --> 00:02:15.290
By the way, USA Today and Harvard

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.353
have proved that you lose one IQ point

00:02:18.353 --> 00:02:22.726
for every hour that you
leave your email on.

00:02:22.726 --> 00:02:25.358
At the end of the day
you've lost ten IQ points.

00:02:25.358 --> 00:02:28.029
You actually become
stupider throughout the day.

00:02:28.029 --> 00:02:29.529
Dumber.

00:02:29.529 --> 00:02:31.925
And I ask this of my audiences, I say,

00:02:31.925 --> 00:02:33.209
Have you ever finished a day

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:34.743
where you don't think you've
accomplished anything?

00:02:34.743 --> 00:02:37.328
You've been on email,
responding to your bings,

00:02:37.328 --> 00:02:39.785
and beeps and rings and so on all day.

00:02:39.785 --> 00:02:41.828
And at the end of the day you go home

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:42.944
and honey says,

00:02:42.944 --> 00:02:43.953
"What do you want for dinner?"

00:02:43.953 --> 00:02:44.786
and you say,

00:02:44.786 --> 00:02:45.619
"I don't know.

00:02:45.619 --> 00:02:46.452
"I don't care.

00:02:46.452 --> 00:02:47.285
"Anything.

00:02:47.285 --> 00:02:48.256
"I just want a drink."

00:02:48.256 --> 00:02:51.779
Because you're so exhausted
you cannot even decide,

00:02:51.779 --> 00:02:53.764
sit there and basically,

00:02:53.764 --> 00:02:57.017
like you've just been punched
in the side of the head.

00:02:57.017 --> 00:02:59.579
Because your brain is dead,

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.309
and you lose ten IQ points.

00:03:01.309 --> 00:03:03.767
You get stupider throughout the day.

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:06.600
You've got to turn that darn thing off

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.772
if you want to remain sharp.

00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:09.728
You develop a habit.

00:03:09.728 --> 00:03:11.631
You say, "I'm going to develop a habit,

00:03:11.631 --> 00:03:13.695
"and I'm going to give myself my reward,

00:03:13.695 --> 00:03:15.965
"and my reward will be to check my email

00:03:15.965 --> 00:03:18.624
"after I finish my first task."

00:03:18.624 --> 00:03:23.200
So all of success in
life is task completion.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.362
Let me repeat that.

00:03:24.362 --> 00:03:26.606
I just had a long conversation
with an entrepreneur

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.221
and he almost fell off his chair.

00:03:28.221 --> 00:03:29.636
I was coaching him.

00:03:29.636 --> 00:03:31.500
And he said he'd never heard that before.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.580
And then I spoke to this group

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.798
I was telling you in Japan,

00:03:34.798 --> 00:03:36.288
I told them the same thing,

00:03:36.288 --> 00:03:38.130
and they were just flabbergasted.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.120
Is the key to success in
life is task completion.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.180
If you don't complete
tasks you have no future.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:46.774
And so if task completion is the key,

00:03:46.774 --> 00:03:49.748
then what you do is complete
more and more important tasks.

00:03:49.748 --> 00:03:51.168
And if you start every day

00:03:51.168 --> 00:03:55.003
by completing the most important task,

00:03:55.003 --> 00:03:57.693
your brain actually releases endorphins.

00:03:57.693 --> 00:03:59.567
Now endorphins is another chemical,

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.511
and it's only released
when you do something

00:04:01.511 --> 00:04:03.328
that is life enhancing.

00:04:03.328 --> 00:04:05.714
And what that means is
when you do something

00:04:05.714 --> 00:04:07.893
that is good for you
that enhances your life,

00:04:07.893 --> 00:04:10.431
that furthers you it makes you happy.

00:04:10.431 --> 00:04:11.907
It releases energy.

00:04:11.907 --> 00:04:14.586
It raises your self-esteem.

00:04:14.586 --> 00:04:16.073
I just want to say,

00:04:16.073 --> 00:04:17.400
if you want to be a winner,

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.332
how to be a winner?

00:04:18.332 --> 00:04:19.438
Well, you win.

00:04:19.438 --> 00:04:21.578
Winning means you cross the finish line.

00:04:21.578 --> 00:04:23.517
So if you start and complete a task

00:04:23.517 --> 00:04:25.259
you're actually winning.

00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:27.681
And you get a feeling of being a winner.

00:04:27.681 --> 00:04:32.054
Which gives you a suffusion
of energy and inspiration.

00:04:32.054 --> 00:04:33.655
And it drives you and motivates you

00:04:33.655 --> 00:04:35.371
to want to get that feeling again.

00:04:35.371 --> 00:04:36.858
So how do you get that feeling again?

00:04:36.858 --> 00:04:38.821
You start and complete another task.

00:04:38.821 --> 00:04:40.085
So I've developed a habit,

00:04:40.085 --> 00:04:42.744
and people who are successful
developed the habit

00:04:42.744 --> 00:04:44.443
of starting and completing tasks.

00:04:44.443 --> 00:04:47.364
So my wife comes in and says
dinner is in five minutes.

00:04:47.364 --> 00:04:48.324
So I look at my list

00:04:48.324 --> 00:04:50.579
and I say okay, there's
a five minute task.

00:04:50.579 --> 00:04:53.324
And I'm going to start and
complete a five minute task.

00:04:53.324 --> 00:04:54.894
And each time you complete a task

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.303
you get a burst of endorphins.

00:04:56.303 --> 00:04:58.222
The bigger the task, the more endorphins.

00:04:58.222 --> 00:05:01.114
The more endorphins, the more
quickly you become addicted

00:05:01.114 --> 00:05:03.024
to starting and completing
important tasks.

00:05:03.024 --> 00:05:06.659
And every single successful
person has a reputation

00:05:06.659 --> 00:05:08.935
for starting and
completing important tasks.

00:05:08.935 --> 00:05:11.379
You want the job done,
give it to him or her.

00:05:11.379 --> 00:05:13.340
You want the product served on time,

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.414
you want the product completed,

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:16.556
you want the product
manufactured, shipped, delivered,

00:05:16.556 --> 00:05:17.389
give it to him.

00:05:17.389 --> 00:05:18.222
Give it to her.

00:05:18.222 --> 00:05:19.055
Give it to that company.

00:05:19.055 --> 00:05:20.597
Cause they always deliver.

00:05:20.597 --> 00:05:22.173
That's the best reputation you can have

00:05:22.173 --> 00:05:24.256
if you want to get rich.

